sieve-filter-v2
; Letter pairs: two letters may stand side by side inside a word only if some word of the
; list has them so (and a word may start or end with a letter only if some word does). It
; needs no dictionary of whole words, so names and new words pass while keyboard-mashing
; mostly does not; at min_words 1 the pairs no word has are: bq bx dx fq fx fz hx jb jc jg jq jv jx jz kq kz mx px qc qd qg qh qj qm qn qp qq qr qt qv qx qy qz sx tx vc vf vj vm vq vw vx wq wx xj zx.
; The start of the unit may be the middle of a word, so its first letter is free. States: 0
; the start, 1 after a SPACE, 2 + n after letter n.
; Generated by tools/build_text_plugins.py from scowl-2020.12.07-en-80-names.txt (sha256 d4aece883446c883591ad8c47ef265af945497fa4105aef6ccc30fd7dbfe2cba).
id        letter-pairs
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  No two letters side by side inside a word that no word of the list has side by side.
param     min_words  int  1  1  10  how many words of the list must have a pair for it to be allowed

states    28
start     0
accept    0..27
